Fillets: the face of a piece walked again past an OnSame end
(WalkedOnSameToEndFace, 0600) is generated by the spine's edges as the
piece it replaces was (mitcad#343).

WalkedOnSameToEndFace walks the stripe's last piece again from its other
end, past the vertex up to the face at the end, and puts the new SurfData
in the old one's place. The edges' map to the surfaces they generate
(myEVIMap) was filled while the stripe was walked and still named the old
piece's surface, which no face is built on any more: Generated() of the
spine's edges left the new piece's face out, and a caller naming the
result's faces from the edges they come from found that face unnamed (a
rounding of a band and a cone ending at a notch wall, whose later
roundings name the edge where the wall cuts it). The old surface's index
is now replaced by the new one's in the map.

Upstream: new.

